In total, 34 genes were found associated with multiple mineral elements. These genes were identified based on SNPs directly associated with multiple mineral elements or located in the overlap between genomic intervals of different SNPs associated with multiple mineral elements, including 5 genes previously associated with ion homeostasis and/or with transporter activity, such as Potri.005G018800 and Potri.005G018700 both identified by two SNP positions found associated with the two heavy metals, Ni and Cd (
Figure 8
;
Supplementary Table S5
). Potri.005G018800 is a homolog of AtCRT1a, a member of the calreticulin protein family, localized in the ER and involved in multiple cellular processes, including calcium homeostasis (
